The task is to implement a Verilog module named `TopModule` that calculates the even parity bit for an 8-bit input. Even parity means the parity bit is the XOR sum of all the input bits.

The implementation uses the reduction XOR operator `^` on the 8-bit input `in`, which correctly computes the XOR of all bits.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input [7:0] in,
    output parity
);
    assign parity = ^in;
endmodule
```
